<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "unraid-disk-event-trigger">
<!ENTITY author    "maxandcheeses">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.08.03.2">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://github.com/maxandcheeses/unraid-disk-event-trigger/raw/main/unraid-disk-event-trigger.plg">
<!ENTITY srcURL     "https://github.com/maxandcheeses/unraid-disk-event-trigger/releases/download/v&version;/unraid-disk-event-trigger.txz">
<!ENTITY srcMD5     "f8b7cd52cf7487a2e3d36c709eb0a123">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" launch="Settings/unraid-disk-event-trigger/unraid-disk-event-trigger.page" min="6.9">

<CHANGES>
###2026.08.03.2
- Fix: icon still didn't show on the plugin's own page (only the Settings/Utilities tile picked it up). That header icon is driven by a separate "Tag" attribute, resolved from &lt;plugin&gt;/icons/&lt;tag&gt; - now set. Verified server-side by invoking Unraid's actual icon-resolving functions against the deployed files before releasing, rather than assuming.

###2026.08.03.1
- Fix: custom plugin icon didn't actually show up. The Settings/Utilities tile grid resolves a .png Icon via &lt;plugin&gt;/images/&lt;icon&gt; (falling back to the plugin root), not &lt;plugin&gt;/icons/&lt;icon&gt; like the top-nav utility buttons do - the icon is now shipped in both locations.

###2026.08.03
- Add: custom disk+thermometer plugin icon, shown in the Utilities menu and the Settings/Plugins listing (previously the built-in generic "temperature" icon).

###2026.08.02.12
- Fix: the delay tooltip was a plain `title` on the number input, which is easy to miss. Replaced with a visible (i) info icon next to each delay field.

###2026.08.02.11
- Add: tooltip on each on/off delay field explaining what it does.

###2026.08.02.10
- Change: the on/off delay is now two independent settings - "Turn ON at" and "Turn OFF at" each have their own delay field shown right next to the temperature, instead of one shared delay for both directions.

###2026.08.02.9
- Add: optional per-rule "turn on/off delay" (seconds). When set, a threshold crossing is only sent once the condition has held continuously for that long; if it reverts before then, the pending change is cancelled. Forced-ON during a parity check/rebuild still fires immediately, bypassing the delay.

###2026.08.02.8
- Add: the YAML backup view is now a writable editor - edit and click "Validate &amp; Apply YAML" to save. Both a YAML syntax parser and structural validation run server-side before anything is written; invalid input is rejected with a specific error and never touches the saved config.
- Change: "View as YAML" is now a toggle (View/Hide), and the download filename is unraid-disk-event-trigger.yaml.

###2026.08.02.7
- Fix: plugin description didn't show up on Settings &gt; Plugins. Unraid's native Plugins page (ShowPlugins.php) reads README.md directly off disk from the installed plugin directory - a previous release wrongly excluded it from the package. Now included again.

###2026.08.02.6
- Fix: "tracked state" badge got reset to unknown whenever a rule was folded/unfolded; now cached and preserved across re-renders.
- Change: badge now shows only "State: ON/OFF/unknown", no temperature, with a clearer visual style.
- Add: top-of-page "Plugin enabled" toggle - when off, the background poller process itself is stopped entirely (not just idled), including across reboots.
- Add: "View as YAML" / download for the current config, for easy backup.
- Fixed the package build to not include README.md or macOS AppleDouble metadata junk files.

###2026.08.02.5
- Fix: Check Device State's MQTT read could time out for devices/bridges (e.g. zigbee2mqtt) that don't retain state and only report on change. Now publishes a "&lt;state_topic&gt;/get" trigger before waiting, prompting an immediate report. Verified against a real Sonoff ZBMicro plug via zigbee2mqtt.
- Add: each rule now shows a live "tracked state" badge (ON/OFF/unknown, with last known temp), refreshed automatically and immediately after Check Device State.

###2026.08.02.4
- Fix: a manual Test ON/OFF didn't update the tracked hysteresis state, so a Test OFF after an automatic ON left the poll cycle believing the relay was still on and it never re-fired.
- Add: per-rule "force_resend" flag to re-send the ON/OFF command every poll cycle even when unchanged, as protection against the device drifting out of sync.
- Add: "Check Device State" button (Tasmota HTTP status query, or an MQTT state topic) that reads the device's actual state without changing anything and self-heals the tracked relay state to match.
- Add: MQTT state-topic JSON parsing is an explicit opt-in checkbox (default off) rather than automatic sniffing.

###2026.08.02.3
- Add: "Clear Log" button (with confirmation prompt) next to Refresh Log.

###2026.08.02.2
- Fix: Save &amp; Apply (and every other write action) silently did nothing, because Unraid's webGUI drops any POST missing a csrf_token. Now wired through correctly.
- Add: show/hide toggle on password fields.
- Add: "Test MQTT Connection" button that checks broker reachability and auth without publishing anything.
- Add: rules collapse by default when there's more than one, stay open when there's exactly one; manual toggle overrides.
- Fix: cramped padding on collapsed rules; labeled the per-rule "Enabled" checkbox.
- All changes verified live via the Chrome extension against an authenticated Unraid session, not just simulated.

###2026.08.02.1
- Fix: .plg install script's heredoc broke XML parsing, causing "XML file doesn't exist or xml parse error" during install.
- Fix: srcURL used the un-prefixed version for the release tag, causing a 404 on the .txz download during install.
- Fix: disk temperature table stayed empty on page load/refresh (get_status returned disks as a JSON object instead of an array).
- All three issues found and fixed by installing and exercising the plugin end-to-end on a real Unraid 7.3.2 box.

###2026.08.02
- Initial release: SMART disk temp monitoring with HTTP/MQTT (Tasmota &amp; zigbee2mqtt) triggers, MQTT username/password auth, and optional forced-on triggers during parity checks and array rebuilds.
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/&name;/&name;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&srcURL;</URL>
<MD5>&srcMD5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/&name;
if [ ! -f /boot/config/plugins/&name;/rules.json ]; then
  printf '%s\n' '{' '    "poll_interval": 60,' '    "rules": []' '}' > /boot/config/plugins/&name;/rules.json
fi
chmod +x /etc/rc.d/rc.unraid-disk-event-trigger
if grep -q '"enabled": *false' /boot/config/plugins/&name;/rules.json 2>/dev/null; then
  echo "Plugin is disabled in saved config, not starting the poller."
else
  /etc/rc.d/rc.unraid-disk-event-trigger restart
fi
echo "unraid-disk-event-trigger installed."
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
/etc/rc.d/rc.unraid-disk-event-trigger stop
removepkg &name;
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
